Use this guide for the shared file setup. It applies to a Windows Dedicated Server and to the Mornedhel Docker images with Proton or Wine. For GPortal, follow [[Multiplayer: Install ShroudForge on GPortal|the GPortal-specific guide]] because its file manager rejects the two ShroudForge executable files.

== Before you change the server ==

Stop the server and make a backup of its world and configuration. Keep a copy of the current container or hosting settings before changing them.

== Find the server installation folder ==

Locate the folder containing <code>enshrouded_server.exe</code>. ShroudForge's files go in this folder, beside the server executable.

For a Windows installation, open the folder used by Steam or your hosting panel.

For the Mornedhel Docker image, inspect the existing container and its mounts. The image uses <code>/opt/enshrouded</code> as the game-files mount. The host path shown as the mount's <code>Source</code> is where you install the files. Confirm the executable's actual location instead of assuming a subfolder:

<pre>
NAME=YOUR_CONTAINER_NAME
docker exec "$NAME" find /opt/enshrouded -name enshrouded_server.exe -print
</pre>

The container may place <code>enshrouded_server.exe</code> below the mounted directory. Use the folder that contains the executable as the install folder.

== Copy ShroudForge ==

Download the [https://github.com/bonsaibauer/shroudforge/releases/latest latest ShroudForge release] and extract the ZIP. Copy all files and folders from the extracted release beside <code>enshrouded_server.exe</code>. Do not copy only the DLLs. The release includes the <code>shroudforge</code> folder and other required files.

== Install a mod ==

Extract the mod package and copy its mod folder into <code>mods</code> beside <code>enshrouded_server.exe</code>. Keep the folder structure and additional files supplied by the mod creator. A typical package looks like this:

<pre>
mods/
└─ my-mod/
   ├─ mod.json
   ├─ extended.mod.json (optional)
   └─ src/mod.lua
</pre>

Install the same mod separately on the client if the mod's instructions or process targets require it. A server installation does not copy the mod to connected players.

== Continue with your server setup ==

* [[Multiplayer: Windows Dedicated Server|Set up a Windows Dedicated Server]].
* [[Multiplayer: Mornedhel Docker server (Proton)|Set up Mornedhel's Docker server with Proton]].
* [[Multiplayer: Mornedhel Docker server (Wine)|Set up Mornedhel's Docker server with Wine]].
* [[Multiplayer: Install ShroudForge on GPortal|Set up ShroudForge on GPortal]].

